skills.prompt:
Improve the overall structure and presentation of this document.

Reorganize content where useful so information appears in a logical order, related ideas are grouped together, and the document is easy to scan and understand.

Improve the use of headings, paragraphs, lists, emphasis, and other available Markdown structure where appropriate.

Also look for opportunities to make better use of the editor components and custom markup described in the available component metadata. Use those components when they provide a clearer, more appropriate, or more useful representation of the existing content.

Do not introduce components merely for decoration. Only use them when they meaningfully improve the document.

You may:
- reorder sections or paragraphs;
- split overly long sections;
- combine redundant sections;
- add, remove, or improve headings;
- convert suitable content into lists or other appropriate structures;
- replace plain Markdown with an available component when the component better expresses the same content.

Preserve the document's meaning, facts, links, and important details. Do not invent new substantive information.
